# L §2.5 (round 12): "At a position keyed by a stepped range (§5.6), a key is a value of the range's type, written or
# computed, and must be one of the range's values, a + i·s <= b for a whole number i >= 0 (LOAD-KEY for a literal,
# RUN-KEY at run)". r is keyed by the days 2026-01-01 + 7·i: its row at 2026-01-08 is one of them (q: 1 there, the `*`
# row's 0 at 2026-01-15; q2 sums 2026-01-01, -08, -15, -22, -29: 1). (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.5, writer 5's T-5.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input r[d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 days]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[2026-01-08] = 1 "s"
  r[*] = 0 "s"

ask q: r[2026-01-08], r[2026-01-15]
ask q2: sum(r[d] for d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-01-31 step 7 days)
=== expect
q: (1, 0)
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 1
  cut 2026-12-31
